        "original_id": "55f7a17f-1cac-548b-bc4d-9ae069820c93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Big Pig, Blur, Grammatics\n- People: Sherine Abeyratne, Damon Albarn, Graham Coxon, Alex James, Dave Rowntree, Tony Antonaides, Neil Baker, Nick Disbray, Tim Rosewarne, Adrian Scaglione, Oleh Witer\n- Places: Australia, Leeds, England\n- Genres: funk, rock, pop, alternative rock\n\nFacts:\n- Big Pig was an Australian funk, rock, and pop band that existed from 1985 to 1991.\n- From 1985 to 1991, Sherine Abeyratne provided lead vocals for Big Pig.\n- An early Big Pig line-up included Sherine Abeyratne, Tony Antonaides, Neil Baker, Nick Disbray, Tim Rosewarne, Adrian Scaglione, and Oleh Witer.\n- Blur consists of Damon Albarn, Graham Coxon, Alex James, and Dave Rowntree.\n- Grammatics was a British alternative rock band from Leeds, England.\n- Grammatics was predominantly influenced by 1990s British bands such as Blur, Pulp, and Suede.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
